WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
Chlorine is a pale green
gas, and it is toxic.

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.720
In the First World War,
it was used as a poison gas.

3
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.220
Yet chlorine goes into drinking water,
and where water is chlorinated,

4
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.460
cholera and typhoid outbreaks
have largely ended.

5
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.540
So why would we put a poison
gas into the water we drink?

6
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:24.220
In this mission, you'll meet the halogens,
from a pale green gas to a dark,

7
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.960
shiny solid, and explain why their
boiling points rise down the group.

8
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.480
Then you'll watch one halogen
push another out of its salts,

9
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.020
and weigh up the benefits
and risks of treating water.

10
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:41.330
Your mission: explain why a gas once used
as a weapon goes into our drinking water.